### A run interrupted by a crash keeps its data
run 6e2cd962a687 started
$ [bench@droplet] kill -9 $(cat ballast-1.0.0/run/ballast.pid); sleep 6; cd ballast-1.0.0 && bin/ballastctl health
healthy: version 1.0.0, up 4 s
(exit 0)
$ [bench@droplet] curl -sS --cacert mycerts/ballast.crt -H 'Authorization: Bearer ****' https://127.0.0.1:8443/api/runs/6e2cd962a687 | ballast-1.0.0/runtime/python/bin/python3 -c 'import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print("status:", d["status"], "| measured seconds kept:", d["analysis"]["summary"]["measured_seconds"], "| ops kept:", d["analysis"]["summary"]["ok"], "|", d["error"]["detail"])'
status: interrupted | measured seconds kept: 12 | ops kept: 2401 | The application stopped while this run was active. Data recorded up to that point is kept.
(exit 0)

### Autostart without root, then restart the whole box
$ [bench@droplet] cd ballast-1.0.0 && bin/ballastctl autostart enable && crontab -l
Added an @reboot entry to your crontab:
  @reboot /home/bench/ballast-1.0.0/bin/ballastctl start
cron runs it at boot; it needs cron to be running on this host (check with: pgrep cron).
@reboot /home/bench/ballast-1.0.0/bin/ballastctl start >/dev/null 2>&1 # ballast-autostart /home/bench/ballast-1.0.0
(exit 0)
$ docker restart droplet
droplet
(exit 0)
